WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
- My name is Guillaume, I am 29 years old,

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.775
and I created an NGO called
Singa in France, starting,

00:00:05.775 --> 00:00:07.552
now it's in six different countries,

00:00:07.552 --> 00:00:11.139
and basically, what we
do is connect refugees

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:14.547
with members of other societies
around stuff that they love

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.714
or on things that they do.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.817
What I'm interested in is innovation,

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:25.417
is also a sense of
justice in our societies,

00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:28.057
and when I started working Australia,

00:00:28.057 --> 00:00:31.655
I started to get in touch
with a lot of refugees

00:00:31.655 --> 00:00:33.821
and asylum seekers, and they told me about

00:00:33.821 --> 00:00:35.323
all the dreams that they had,

00:00:35.323 --> 00:00:39.016
and I realized that nobody
was actually interested

00:00:39.016 --> 00:00:42.112
in that kind of issues, they
were always taking about

00:00:42.112 --> 00:00:46.195
admin, about the legal
aspects of seeking asylum.

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:49.310
But nobody was talking
about how you unlock

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.793
the potential of people,
and how you rebuild

00:00:51.793 --> 00:00:54.043
the potential in a society.

00:00:55.346 --> 00:00:58.711
What we're trying to
achieve is to make sure that

00:00:58.711 --> 00:01:01.792
local people actually really understand

00:01:01.792 --> 00:01:04.253
what they're going through and

00:01:04.253 --> 00:01:07.859
what they could do about it.

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:10.695
And it's really about crowdsourcing,

00:01:10.695 --> 00:01:13.208
because it's more important
to actually meet someone

00:01:13.208 --> 00:01:15.191
who works in the same field than you

00:01:15.191 --> 00:01:18.983
than to go ten times to the job center.

00:01:18.983 --> 00:01:21.610
One of the biggest
challenges, the fact that it's

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:25.681
a really political topic,
so when I started saying,

00:01:25.681 --> 00:01:28.389
it's about citizenship
and it's about innovation

00:01:28.389 --> 00:01:30.542
and it's about a lot of different things,

00:01:30.542 --> 00:01:32.379
people always go back to, y'know,

00:01:32.379 --> 00:01:36.111
a debate about whether
refugees are welcome or not.

00:01:36.111 --> 00:01:37.390
And I think that's not the question,

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.833
the question is how you
make sure that if you have

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.114
people on your territory, you create

00:01:42.114 --> 00:01:44.390
connections with locals, but also,

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:48.557
you make sure that they can
contribute to that society.

00:01:49.751 --> 00:01:52.532
Today, Singa exists in
four cities in France,

00:01:52.532 --> 00:01:55.414
but we have people telling
us, we want to start

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:58.111
your organization in Bedoin, Ajain,

00:01:58.111 --> 00:01:59.799
in a lot of different cities.

00:01:59.799 --> 00:02:02.837
So, we're changing our job,
we have been for a long time.

00:02:02.837 --> 00:02:04.576
People who were organizing events,

00:02:04.576 --> 00:02:07.159
people were connecting ourself,

00:02:08.704 --> 00:02:10.503
and now we are going to be supporting

00:02:10.503 --> 00:02:12.898
local people who do that.

00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:14.968
So the idea is to be present

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:18.551
in thousands of cities in 2020.

00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:22.569
The fact that every day
I'm learning something,

00:02:22.569 --> 00:02:26.778
the fact that every day
I'm meeting with a chef,

00:02:26.778 --> 00:02:29.610
an engineer, that's why
I'm continuing this,

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:30.693
it's amazing.

